    "## Calibration concept\n",
    "\n",
    "The detector does not measure the true beam energy directly. Instead, it records a **detected energy** from the energy deposited in its sensitive components. To convert this detector response into an estimate of the particle energy, a simple calibration factor is introduced.\n",
    "\n",
    "The calibration constant is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "C = \\left\\langle \\frac{E_{\\text{true}}}{E_{\\text{detected}}} \\right\\rangle\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where the average is taken over a set of calibration events.\n",
    "\n",
    "The calibrated energy for each event is then calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "E_{\\text{calibrated}} = C \\, E_{\\text{detected}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "To evaluate the performance of this calibration, the fractional residual is defined as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\frac{E_{\\text{calibrated}} - E_{\\text{true}}}{E_{\\text{true}}}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The detector resolution is taken as the standard deviation of this fractional residual over many events.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this project, only events with sufficiently large detected energy are used when calculating $C$, in order to avoid unstable values caused by events with almost zero detector response."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "44fd6848-ba34-482a-b765-f3df2611e1d6",
